{
  "why": "First ML-5 attempt, killed at epoch 42. Plain NLL (beta=0, the paper's Eq.1 as written) degenerated: sigma^2 collapsed onto its per-channel floor everywhere, turning the loss into a fixed weighted MSE with per-channel weights 1/(2*obs_var) = [154, 5, 67, 11905]. vx carries 58.7% of the total error and had the smallest weight, coming out +203% worse than b0; full-state blind RMSE was +52%. Fixed by beta-NLL (--nll-beta 1), which rescales the mean's gradient to MSE's without changing what sigma^2 is fitted to. Kept as the negative result behind that flag.",
